## Reproduction

### Option 1: OSS-Fuzz harness

Run the `assimp_fuzzer` target with the attached test case. It will time out after the configured timeout (default 25s).
[assimp_crash.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26914391/assimp_crash.zip)

### Option 2: Standalone C++ reproducer

Save the triggering input as `pov.bin`, then compile and run:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <assimp/Importer.hpp>
#include <assimp/scene.h>
#include <assimp/postprocess.h>

int main(int argc, char* argv[]) {
    std::string filename = "pov.bin";
    if (argc > 1) {
        filename = argv[1];
    }

    std::cout << "[*] Attempting to read file: " << filename << std::endl;

    Assimp::Importer importer;
    const aiScene* scene = importer.ReadFile(filename,
        aiProcess_CalcTangentSpace       |
        aiProcess_Triangulate            |
        aiProcess_JoinIdenticalVertices  |
        aiProcess_SortByPType);

    if (!scene) {
        std::cerr << "[!] Import failed: " << importer.GetErrorString() << std::endl;
    } else {
        std::cout << "[+] Import successful (bug not reproduced)" << std::endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

The process will hang indefinitely on `importer.ReadFile()`.

## Severity

**Denial of Service**

Any application parsing untrusted OFF files via Assimp can be hung with a crafted input. Relevant for any tool, game engine, or web service that accepts user-uploaded 3D model files.
